      "content": "That's a good start, definitely has some nice imagery.\n\nI just ran it through the preview tool and the Descriptive Richness score is actually kinda low for what we need to hit the homepage. We usually aim for a much higher density of descriptions to make it feel \"premium.\" \n\nCan you expand this into a few more paragraphs? Really lean into the sensory details—the smells, the textures, the feelings. Just try to make it as dense and descriptive as possible so that SEO score really pops. I don't want it to feel forced, just... really, really rich with adjectives.",
